00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:30.080
This right here, this is my old

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:32.159
apartment. This is where it all started.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:35.759
I was working a developer job at a small

00:01:32.159 --> 00:01:38.560
startup. Six figures, stable, but I

00:01:35.759 --> 00:01:41.759
wasn't happy. Something was missing. Not

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:44.320
because the job was bad, but because I

00:01:41.759 --> 00:01:46.399
wasn't building something that was mine.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:48.399
In this apartment right up here, I

00:01:46.399 --> 00:01:50.560
started thinking. [music] I would come

00:01:48.399 --> 00:01:52.560
home every night after work and knew

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:55.439
that I wanted to build something, but I

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:57.600
wasn't able to actually execute on it.

00:01:55.439 --> 00:02:00.880
And this haunted me [music] for months

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:04.840
until I found a very special place. And

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:04.840
I want to take you there right now.

00:02:06.416 --> 00:02:08.436
[music]

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.986
[music]

00:02:18.319 --> 00:02:23.920
This right here used to be a Starbucks.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:26.560
It's closed now. And I guess that's kind

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:28.800
of fitting. I'd sit right there every

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:31.280
single morning and put in two hours of

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.920
deep work before I started my job. I'd

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:35.519
get my coffee. I'd get my laptop and I

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:37.760
started building something. I was

00:02:35.519 --> 00:02:40.080
writing. I was coding. I was sending

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:41.840
emails. I was interviewing founders.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:44.800
Nobody in there had any idea what I was

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:47.680
doing. And honestly, I didn't either. It

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:50.239
wasn't impressive at all, but it was

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:52.720
consistent. I kept coming back every

00:02:50.239 --> 00:02:55.599
single day refreshing Stripe, watching

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:58.560
it go from zero to a couple hundred

00:02:55.599 --> 00:03:00.879
bucks. I know it sounds small, but that

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:03.519
was everything to me. And the only

00:03:00.879 --> 00:03:08.360
question I could ask myself was, what

00:03:03.519 --> 00:03:08.360
would happen if I went all in?

00:03:12.159 --> 00:03:17.120
>> This is the walk I would do every single

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:19.120
morning on my way to work for a year.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:21.120
daydreaming, thinking about what it

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:24.080
would be like to build my own thing

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:26.080
until one day it felt like too much. And

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:28.480
I had to make a decision that would

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:31.519
change the rest of my life. This right

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:33.200
here, this is my old job. And I'll never

00:03:31.519 --> 00:03:35.840
forget the day where I worked up the

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:38.400
courage to walk in there, quit that job,

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:41.200
