00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:21.759
I'm tired and ready to move on? I wish I

00:06:19.039 --> 00:06:23.919
had an answer right now, but I honestly

00:06:21.759 --> 00:06:26.800
don't know. But anyways, looks like it's

00:06:23.919 --> 00:06:29.039
that time.

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:32.080
As I walked toward that office, I kept

00:06:29.039 --> 00:06:35.440
thinking about the cage. How something I

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:36.880
built for freedom slowly took it away.

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:40.080
>> 8 minutes left, guys.

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:43.039
>> And I asked myself, am I still building

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:45.360
or am I just holding on? Holding it so

00:06:43.039 --> 00:06:48.240
close because I was afraid of what it

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:50.800
would mean to lose it. afraid of who I

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:53.680
would be [music] without it. And in that

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:56.240
moment, I realized something. The goal

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:59.440
was never just money. It was to build

00:06:56.240 --> 00:07:01.199
something bigger than myself, something

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:04.319
real, [music] something that didn't

00:07:01.199 --> 00:07:07.199
